en these conditions hold true and no control request is outstanding (`reader.cljc:710`).\n6. **Input conflict**: Confirmed. Handled natively in `settle-answer` (`reader.cljc:552`). It ends the run with `:cause :input-conflict` and avoids quarantining or misclassifying as `:intent-conflict`.\n7. **Empty-path hazard sweep (D11 defect class)**: Confirmed fixed. `rewrite-held` correctly routes around the root's empty `ap` with an explicit `(if (seq ap) (update-in r ap rewrite) (rewrite r))` (`reader.cljc:340`). An exhaustive sweep verifies all other path updates are safe: `apply-candidate` uses the identical empty-path bypass (`reader.cljc:297`), `ended` safely delegates to vector-appending `(conj ap :yin.k/gate)` (`reader.cljc:99`), and operations hardcoded to static path `[:yin.k/custody :input :next]` remain inherently immune.\n8. **Seam rules and judgment calls**: Confirmed. No transport vocabulary bleeds into the namespace. Both judgment calls—accepting the test-authored gap re-read for the row-5 divergent leg and the opaque request ID in the input-conflict fixture—are architecturally sound and accepted. The code delegates cleanly to the supplied observer and appender interfaces.\n","duration_seconds":143.064682,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":99087,"output_tokens":13085,"thinking_tokens":11404,"cache_read_tokens":268693,"total_tokens":112172}}
